# A path write replaces the fragment of the field (the book, #frame-and-graph-assignment: «Replacing one cell's
# fragment does not implicitly replace the other cell's fragment»). Holder's slot 0 refers to the same fragment as
# Source\x; `Source\x := 9` replaces Source's fragment only: Source x 9, Holder keeps x 1.
(
    Holder:
        int: h 0
    Source:
        int: x 1
)
sub: main ()
    @: shared node[0]
    shared\Holder[0] := @(shared\Source\x)
    shared\Source\x := 9
main()
